Q: Google maps night mode embed iframe A: <p>In Next.JS is it:</p>
<pre><code> &lt;svg style={{ position: 'absolute', width: 0, height: 0 }}&gt;
                            &lt;filter id=&quot;smart-invert-dark&quot; x=&quot;-10%&quot; y=&quot;-10%&quot; width=&quot;120%&quot; height=&quot;120%&quot; colorInterpolationFilters=&quot;sRGB&quot;&gt;
                                &lt;feColorMatrix type=&quot;matrix&quot;
                                    values=&quot;0.2126 0.7152 0.0722 0 0
                                            0.2126 0.7152 0.0722 0 0
                                            0.2126 0.7152 0.0722 0 0
                                            0 0 0 1 0&quot;
                                    result=&quot;gray&quot; /&gt;

                                &lt;feComposite in=&quot;SourceGraphic&quot; in2=&quot;gray&quot; operator=&quot;arithmetic&quot; k2=&quot;1&quot; k3=&quot;-1&quot; result=&quot;colorOnly&quot; /&gt;

                                &lt;feComponentTransfer in=&quot;gray&quot; result=&quot;invGray&quot;&gt;
                                    &lt;feFuncR type=&quot;table&quot; tableValues=&quot;0.65 0.05&quot; /&gt;
                                    &lt;feFuncG type=&quot;table&quot; tableValues=&quot;0.65 0.05&quot; /&gt;
                                    &lt;feFuncB type=&quot;table&quot; tableValues=&quot;0.65 0.05&quot; /&gt;
                                &lt;/feComponentTransfer&gt;

                                &lt;feComposite in=&quot;invGray&quot; in2=&quot;colorOnly&quot; operator=&quot;arithmetic&quot; k2=&quot;1&quot; k3=&quot;1&quot; result=&quot;final&quot; /&gt;

                            &lt;/filter&gt;
                        &lt;/svg&gt;

&lt;iframe
                            style={{
                                filter: 'url(#smart-invert-dark)',
                                imageRendering: '-webkit-optimize-contrast',
                                transform: 'translateZ(0.0001)',
                                backfaceVisibility: 'hidden'
                            }}
                            src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?...&quot;
                            allowFullScreen=&quot;&quot;
                            loading=&quot;lazy&quot;
                            referrerPolicy=&quot;no-referrer-when-downgrade&quot;
                        /&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: Get the TimeZone using CountryCode + CityName A: <p>As it occured there was no <code>null</code> from the code of getting the <code>TimeZone</code> using <code>CountryCode</code> &amp; <code>CityName</code> and this code snippet works as expected with output: <strong>America/New_York</strong></p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code> var city = &quot;New_York&quot;;

 var zones = TzdbDateTimeZoneSource.Default.ZoneLocations;

 var countryCode = &quot;US&quot;;

 var zoneForCityAndCountryCode = zones
     .FirstOrDefault(z =&gt; z.CountryCode == countryCode &amp;&amp; z.ZoneId.EndsWith(city, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
     ?.ZoneId;


 Console.WriteLine(zoneForCityAndCountryCode); // America/New_York
</code></pre>

Q: Android Paging 3 doesnt show Loadstate Adapter A: <p>Try to override the following method in your ProductLoadingStateAdapter like this:</p>
<pre><code>class ProductLoadingStateAdapter: LoadStateAdapter&lt;XXX&gt;() {
   override fun onBindViewholder...

   override fun onCreateViewHolder...

   override fun displayLoadStateAsItem(loadState: LoadState): Boolean {
      return loadState is LoadState.Loading || loadState is LoadState.Error || loadState is LoadState.NotLoading
   }
}
</code></pre>
<p>If you look into the source code of LoadStateAdapter, it only emits Loading and Error load states to the adapter by default, which means the adapter won't know if the loading process has finished.</p>
<p>So in your case, the following code will always results <code>progress.visibility</code> to be <code>VISIBLE</code>. Because you can only get <code>LoadState.Loading</code> state in your <code>onBindViewHolder</code>.</p>
<pre><code>//loadState is always LoadState.Loading
if (loadState is LoadState.Loading) progress.visibility =
            View.VISIBLE; txtErrorMessage.visibility = View.GONE
</code></pre>
